  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.3. Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement policies for a just transition towards environmentally sustainable economies and societies</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Employment and Social Affairs in consultation with the Seychelles Federation Workers Union (SFWU), the Seychelles Chamber of Commerce and Industry (SCCI), the General Employer Trade Union in Seychelles (GETUS) adopted a tripartite agreement which is a policy measure to promote decent work in blue economy. This agreement was developed and adopted by the sub-committee on Just Transition put in place in March 2023 under the National Consultative Committee on Employment (NCCE), which is the structure for social dialogue at national level given the importance of blue economy for the country. With the contribution of the SDGs Funds, the ILO supported the Ministry of Employment in setting up the sub-committee on Just Transition under the National Consultative Committee on Employment (NCCE). The ILO also conveyed a capacity building and consultation meeting with constituents in March 2023 to discuss on the best way to put in place a social dialogue mechanism  on just transition from which the option to create the sub-committee was decided. The ILO also supported the Sub-committee to draft the tripartite agreement to promote decent work in blue economy.

The results of the skills need assessment on how to promote decent work and sustainable entrepreneurship in the field of circular economy undertaken by ILO in 2023 will be used to inform the social dialogue on Just Transition.</narrative>
   </description>
